1952..2026 Comment "/// A path at every loop whose inverse arm drops its rest\'s path: each arm"
2027..2108 Comment "/// checks at its letter, but at `loop ∷ back(loop) ∷ q` the loop arm carries"
2109..2194 Comment "/// the inverse arm\'s reflexivity to `Path.here(loop ∷ back(loop) ∷ q)`, which is"
2195..2270 Comment "/// not the path at `q` the cancellation\'s right side reads. Read as a set,"
2271..2339 Comment "/// the loops would identify the two; the words are not read as one."
